      "source_text": "Because $T-40=10z_1$ and $d-0.5=0.1z_2$, the target is $u_*(z)=0.4z_1+0.002z_2$. Its gradient norm is $\\sqrt{0.4^2+0.002^2}\\approx0.400005\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$ per normalized input unit. On an open region, increments in that gradient direction attain this slope, exceeding 0.3. Exact matching is impossible under the chosen budget. Options include reducing the target response or revisiting the downstream sensitivity allowance; changing the training loss cannot remove the contradiction.",
